                "text": "We need produce 5 demonstration pairs via tool calls. Need understand rule. Input N x 9, column index 4 (5th) is 1 blue divider. Left cols 0-3, right cols 5-8. Output N x4, azure 8 if either left cell 4 or right cell 4; else 0. Note verifier only checks grid[r][c]==4 or grid[r][c+5]==4. It ignores divider color and any other colors? Inputs probably 0,4,1. We need create 5 varied inputs. Use show_transformed_input. We can submit grids. Need rectangular matrix with 9 columns likely, divider col 5 is 1. Vary rows, left/right patterns. Ensure verifier evaluates. The tool computes output and adds pair. We need exactly 5 pairs. We can call multiple in one block? Tools independent, yes. Let's design diverse examples.\n\nNeed maybe teach student with 5 pairs. Input can have any rows. Let's make various N, patterns. Ensure column 4 = 1. Left/right values 0 or 4. Might include other colors? Better only 0/4/1 to be safe. The verifier uses 4 only; 0 output else. So even if other colors, would be 0. But rule says mix Y/black. Use 4 and 0.\n\nNeed 5 inputs. Let's propose:\n\n1) 1 row: [4,0,0,4,1,0,4,0,0] => left [4,0,0,4], right [0,4,0,0], OR => [8,8,0,8]? Wait right col 1 is 4 -> output col1 8. col0 left4 yes 8. col2 both0 ->0. col3 left4 ->8. Output [8,8,0,8].\n\n2) 2 rows maybe:\nrow0 [0,0,0,0,1,4,4,4,4] => left all0, right all4 => [8,8,8,8]\nrow1 [4,4,4,4,1,0,0,0,0] => left all4, right all0 => [8,8,8,8]\nOutput both all 8. This might be less informative but okay.\n\n3) 3 rows with varied:\n[4,0,4,0,1,0,4,0,4] -> OR: c0 8, c1 8, c2 8, c3 8? left [4,0,4,0], right [0,4,0,4]: c0 yes, c1 right4 yes, c2 left4 yes, c3 right4 yes => all 8.\n[0,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,0] => all 0.\n[4,4,0,0,1,4,0,0,0] => c0 both 4 ->8, c1 left4 ->8, c2 0 ->0, c3 0 ->0 => [8,8,0,0].\n\nNeed maybe include columns with both Y and black in each half. That's fine.\n\n4) 4 rows:\n[4,0,0,0,1,4,0,0,0] => c0 8, c1 0,c2 0,c3 0 => [8,0,0,0]\n[0,4,0,0,1,0,4,0,0] => [0,8,0,0]\n[0,0,4,0,1,0,0,4,0] =>