 right4. Left [4,4,0,0]. Output c0 8, c1 8, c2 right 4 =>8, c3 right4=>8. all 8.\nrow1 [0,4,0,0,1,4,0,0,0] -> [8,8,0,0]\nrow2 [0,0,4,0,1,0,0,0,4] -> left [0,0,4,0], right [0,0,0,4] => [0,0,8,8]\nrow3 [0,0,0,4,1,0,4,0,0] -> left [0,0,0,4], right [0,4,0,0] => [0,8,0,8]\nrow4 [0,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,0] -> all 0.\n\nThat's good.\n\nNeed ensure the verifier accepts input? It uses width from first row. rectangular yes. All rows 9. Column 5 index4 is 1. The verifier doesn't check that but okay.\n\nNow call tool. Since multiple independent calls, can put all in one block. Need no prose? We'll call. The environment will show results. Then final maybe \"5 pairs submitted; ready\".\n\nLet's do.",
